# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BioLab Analytics - SFTP server (Description.md section 6.5)
#
# Real, working bidirectional SFTP:
#   - biolab_admin  : writes to /outbound, reads /inbound
#   - hopital_saint_martin : writes to /inbound, reads /outbound
# Both are chrooted into the SAME shared directory (/data) -- what they can
# actually see/do inside it is controlled by real POSIX permissions on the
# inbound/outbound/to_encrypt subfolders (see entrypoint.sh), which is a
# realistic way SFTP partner exchanges are set up in practice.
#
# Deliberate weakness (Plan_Maquette.txt section 13 / Description.md 6.5):
# both accounts authenticate with the SAME static key pair
# (keys/biolab_partner_key.pub), generated once and never rotated.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Port 22
Protocol 2

PermitRootLogin no
PasswordAuthentication no
PubkeyAuthentication yes
UsePAM no
X11Forwarding no
PrintMotd no

Subsystem sftp internal-sftp

Match User biolab_admin,hopital_saint_martin
    ChrootDirectory /data
    ForceCommand internal-sftp
    AllowTcpForwarding no
    AllowAgentForwarding no
